    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0157" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.24/872: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Boal</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-27T22:00:00-04:00">September 27, 1943—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1197. Your 1567, September 22, 7 p.m.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d138-f1"/> The
                    Department is making no change in export control procedure as regards Bolivia.
                    Decentralization Plan A will continue for the present in full effect in
                    Bolivia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d138-f1" n="50" xml:id="d138-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; in this telegram the Ambassador reiterated the preference of the
                    Bolivian Country Agency for Alternative I and its acceptance of Alternative III
                    only if time were allowed to apply new import and exchange controls.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
